            <div xml:id="d72">

                <pb facs="0117" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48/5046: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-20T11:00:00-04:00">August 20, 1941—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3240. Your 3615, August 13, 9 p.m. and 3637, August 14, 6 p.m.<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d72-f1"/> Please inform Mr. Eden that we have taken note of the
                    revised language of paragraph number 5 relating to shipping, that it seems
                    adequately to cover the point made in our earlier comment, and that we have no
                    further comment to make.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d72-f1" n="24" xml:id="d72-f1-content">
